From 6a08a2814e9c2dea71a97bf070b879251a804ae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ShorterKing <84120105+ShorterKing@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:19:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] econet-eth: update to Git HEAD (2026-10-14)

9644850 Merge pull request #12 from EmreYavuzalp/econet-eth-tx-fixes
f756396 econet-eth: pad short TX frames before handing them to QDMA
a955371 econet-eth: poll TX completions with an hrtimer, don't trust the IRQ
f84e3fe econet-eth: disable the bootloader's CPU-protection rate limiter
bcc4062 econet-eth: fix TX done-queue interrupt stall, cut completion latency
9dc4685 econet-eth: wake all TX queues on completion, fix permanent stall
b3d66a2 econet-eth: raise BQL min limit, TX was serialized to one packet
9f70de5 econet-eth: clear tx_int_delay so TX completions are not throttled
73c78f5 Merge pull request #10 from Cris7015/fix-txbusy-uaf
a2adcbf en75_dev_xmit: don't free the skb on -EBUSY before returning NETDEV_TX_BUSY

With the old version, a Nokia G-140W-C (EN7526G) sent at only about
14 Mbit/s, both when routing and from local sockets: TX completions
arrived late, BQL clamped each TX queue to about two packets, and TCP saw
about 0.4% loss from the resulting queue drops. Raising the BQL floor by
hand then hit the -EBUSY use-after-free and hung the device.
